Fri Oct 16 14:25:32 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.9.91:
  * Security: Fortran capital-F sources no longer feed
    #include directives to cpp, closing arbitrary host-file
    reads into graph.json and LLM context
  * Security: --watch snippets read the trusted scan-root
    file instead of interpolating INPUT_PATH into shell;
    Terraform secret redaction covers variable/output values
  * Language coverage: new EJS and Jinja extractors; SQL
    triggers, Groovy enums, OCaml/Elixir/Fortran/Julia/Kotlin
    structural depth; cross-repo member-call resolution
  * Resolution accuracy: self/this/super bind to the caller's
    own class chain; unqualified calls prefer own-class scope
  * Deterministic, portable graph.json: node ids no longer
    leak checkout path, username, or line endings
  * MCP retrieval much faster (cached traversal graphs);
    query/explain exit codes and truncation hints; hook-guard
    for Pi, OpenCode 2 plugin support, automatic stale-skill
    refresh
  * Raise python-tree-sitter runtime floor to >= 0.25 for
    ABI 15 grammars
  * %check: skip tests needing newer tree-sitter grammars
    than Factory ships (JS tagged-template clash file, one
    PHP blanking test that segfaults the older parser)
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release
    notes for the full list

